      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In England, only 30% of patients with established coronary heart disease (CHD) and raised serum lipids, and fewer than 4% of individuals eligible for primary prevention, receive lipid-lowering therapy. Target total cholesterol concentrations are achieved in fewer than 50% of patients who do receive such treatment. Here, we review the use of statin therapy in the prevention of CHD events."},
      "ArticleTitle": "Statin therapy--what now?",
